From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:38:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: delete only the RX NAPIs that were added

mt76_dma_init() does not add the NAPI of a WED RRO queue, and
mt7996_dma_rro_start() adds it only when WED is not active, but
mt76_dma_cleanup() calls netif_napi_del() for every RX queue. With WED
active, netif_napi_del() then locks the NULL device of a NAPI that was
never added, and mt7996e module removal panics.

Nicolas Cavallari's upstream fix skipped the deletion by the WED RRO
queue role, and also disabled every RX NAPI in the shared cleanup path.
It was reverted because mt7921 and mt7925 already disable their NAPIs,
and a second napi_disable() hangs.

Use NAPI_STATE_LISTED, which netif_napi_del() itself tests, to delete
only the NAPIs that were added. Walk the whole NAPI array, as
mt7996_unregister_device() does to disable them, rather than the queues
with descriptors. This also handles a mt7996 without WED, where the RRO
queues have their NAPIs added.

Fixes: 7dd72bbd6f51 ("wifi: mt76: Fix memory leak destroying device")
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/332bbe9b2784bea2fd2b00fceb8eacf0fba06728
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/6d1c6a758a4c0a690ee56cb849387dfa262fdb17
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 dma.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/dma.c
+++ b/dma.c
@@ -1215,10 +1215,14 @@ void mt76_dma_cleanup(struct mt76_dev *d
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dev->q_mcu); i++)
 		mt76_dma_tx_cleanup(dev, dev->q_mcu[i], true);
 
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dev->napi); i++) {
+		if (test_bit(NAPI_STATE_LISTED, &dev->napi[i].state))
+			netif_napi_del(&dev->napi[i]);
+	}
+
 	mt76_for_each_q_rx(dev, i) {
 		struct mt76_queue *q = &dev->q_rx[i];
 
-		netif_napi_del(&dev->napi[i]);
 		mt76_dma_rx_cleanup(dev, q);
 
 		page_pool_destroy(q->page_pool);
